# English: editing.feature · 简体中文: editing.zh-CN.feature
Feature: Notebook editing
  The user can change a saved entry's meaning, expression, language, notes, tags and starred flag, and maintain the notebook as their own study material.

  Background:
    Given the notebook already contains the English expression "follow up"
    And the entry has a meaning generated by the model

  Rule: The user can edit the meaning, and regenerating overwrites it unconditionally
    Scenario: Rewrite the meaning
      When the user rewrites the meaning in their own words and restarts the app
      Then the entry shows the rewritten meaning

    Scenario: A rewritten meaning is overwritten by regenerating
      Given the user has rewritten the entry's meaning
      When the user triggers regenerating the meaning
      Then the meaning returned by the model replaces the user's rewrite
      And no confirmation appears

  Rule: Notes are stored separately from the meaning, and automatic flows never touch them
    Scenario: Regenerating the meaning leaves the notes alone
      Given the user has written notes for the entry
      When the user triggers regenerating the meaning
      Then the meaning is updated
      And the notes stay as they were

    Scenario: Filling in the meaning on save does not write to the notes
      Given the user saves hand-selected content that has no contextual meaning
      When the meaning is filled in automatically after saving
      Then the notes are still empty

  Rule: Expression and language are editable; a change that collides with an existing entry in the same language is rejected
    Scenario: Remove extra characters from the expression
      When the user changes the expression from "follow up." to "follow up"
      Then the entry's expression is updated
      And the entry's contexts and meaning are unchanged

    Scenario: Correct a misdetected language
      Given the notebook already contains the expression "手紙" marked as Chinese
      When the user changes the entry's language to Japanese
      Then it is still the same entry, with its contexts unchanged

    Scenario: Renaming collides with an existing entry in the same language
      Given the notebook already contains the English expressions "bandwidth" and "bandwith"
      When the user changes "bandwith" to "bandwidth"
      Then the change is rejected with the reason given
      And both entries keep their original values

  Rule: Edits take effect immediately, with no save confirmation
    Scenario: Notes remain after switching entries
      When the user types into the notes, selects another entry and comes back
      Then the notes show what was just typed
      And there is no save button and no "unsaved changes" state

  Rule: Tags are free text, and previously used tags appear while typing
    Scenario: Reuse an existing tag
      Given another entry already has the tag "work"
      When the user starts typing a tag for "follow up"
      Then "work" appears among the suggestions

    Scenario: A new tag
      When the user types the never-used tag "interview" and confirms
      Then the entry has the tag "interview"

    Scenario: A tag disappears with its last entry
      Given only one entry has the tag "interview"
      When the user deletes that entry
      Then "interview" no longer appears in any suggestion or filter

  Rule: Entries can be starred
    Scenario: The star persists
      When the user stars "follow up" and restarts the app
      Then the entry is still shown as starred
